  "name": "leptos-book",
  "description": "A comprehensive technical manual for the Leptos framework, focusing on high-performance Rust web development through fine-grained reactivity and isomorphic execution. It elucidates complex system behaviors such as hydration, islands architecture, and the lifecycle of reactive primitives within a shared graph. The source utilizes mdBook with custom preprocessors to facilitate a structured exploration of server-side rendering and progressive enhancement strategies.",
